# kex: check-only
# A member read on an optional is judged by its value's type (kexhq/kex#699).
# `names` is a field of Culture.TimeSettings, not of Culture.Culture, so on a
# `Culture?` it is as undefined as on a `Culture`; that some other record has
# it let the read through, to fail at run time. A field the value does have
# is reported once, with the advice to map over the optional, and not again
# as a call to an unrelated `name : Weekday -> String`.

main do
  IO.inspect(Culture.of("hu-HU").names)
  IO.inspect(Culture.of("hu-HU").name)
  IO.inspect(Culture.of("hu-HU").map { |c| c.name })
end
